### Changed

- Update the grouped NuGet dependencies with three minor and patch updates. ([#328](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/328))

### Added

- **Breaking:** Remove pull request descriptions from `changelog.json` schema version 2, retaining complete facts in the run record. ([#294](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/294))
- **Breaking:** Show facts and planned model requests in `preview` instead of renderings, without calling a model or requiring a key. ([#292](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/292))
- Report generation outcomes in the first line of the run summary, including review flags and audience failures. ([#342](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/342))
- Group `doctor` checks by Repository, Model and GitHub, with verdicts that explain whether warnings prevent a run. ([#341](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/341))
- Add terminal-aware run progress with the Quiet Pulse spinner and a `--plain` option for plain output. ([#340](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/340))
- Quote pull request text between tags in model prompts, truncating descriptions beyond 8,000 characters without changing the stored facts. ([#338](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/338))
- Prevent `generate` from replacing published release notes unless `--replace-published` is supplied. ([#335](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/335))
- Show a version-tagged configuration template link when `doctor` finds no `chartula.yaml`. ([#329](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/329))
- Show run progress on stderr while reading pull requests, rendering audiences and checking renderings. ([#297](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/297))
- Add `chartula doctor` to check repository, configuration, model and GitHub setup before a generation run. ([#295](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/295))
- Populate `linkedIssues` from the text the model reads at every `factBase.depth`. ([#293](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/293))
- Include non-merge commits without merged pull requests alongside pull request changes in release range order. ([#291](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/291))
- Add `chartula --version` to print the installed informational version without requiring repository setup or credentials. ([#286](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/286))
- Support releases from the first commit through the first tag, requiring confirmation for first-tag and large ranges. ([#282](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/282))

### Fixed

